#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Orb setup for OneDriveRcloneMenubar.
#
# This is a macOS 26 SwiftUI/AppKit menu-bar app. The Linux orb cannot compile
# it, so there is no toolchain to install here. Builds, tests, and runs happen on
# the thread's macOS Satellite. Setup only records that workflow for agents.
set -euo pipefail

guidance_file="$HOME/.config/amp/AGENTS.md"
begin_marker="<!-- onedrive-rclone-mac-menubar orb guidance: begin -->"
end_marker="<!-- onedrive-rclone-mac-menubar orb guidance: end -->"

mkdir -p "$(dirname "$guidance_file")"
touch "$guidance_file"

# Drop any previous copy of this block so reruns converge on the current text.
tmp="$(mktemp)"
awk -v b="$begin_marker" -v e="$end_marker" '
  $0 == b { skip = 1; next }
  $0 == e { skip = 0; next }
  !skip
' "$guidance_file" > "$tmp"

cat >> "$tmp" <<EOF
$begin_marker
# OneDriveRcloneMenubar in an orb

- This is a macOS-only SwiftUI app. The Linux orb cannot build or test it; run all Swift and Xcode commands on the macOS Satellite (\`mac_sidecar start\`, then \`mac_shell\`). The default \`macos-27\` image (Xcode 27.2) builds it.
- Build the app bundle: \`xcodebuild -project OneDriveRcloneMenubar.xcodeproj -scheme OneDriveRcloneMenubar -configuration Debug -derivedDataPath .build/xcode CODE_SIGNING_ALLOWED=NO build\`
- Run the tests: \`swift test\`
- Run the app: \`open .build/xcode/Build/Products/Debug/OneDriveRcloneMenubar.app\`. It is an agent app (\`LSUIElement\`), so it has no Dock icon or window; its status item appears at the right of the menu bar 5 to 15 seconds after launch, so wait or retry the screenshot before concluding it failed. With no rclone configured it shows the \`pause.circle\` (Disabled) icon.
- Screenshot with \`screencapture -x /private/tmp/shot-1.png\` and fetch it with \`mac_read_file\`. The display is 1280x800 points at 2x, so crop the menu bar with \`screencapture -x -R 600,0,680,30 /private/tmp/menubar-1.png\`.
- To test syncing, run \`brew install rclone\` and then \`scripts/setup-fake-onedrive.sh\` on the Satellite. It configures the app against a fake OneDrive, which is an rclone alias remote over a local directory, synced with a second local directory. Then launch the app, choose Resync… and confirm it once, and choose Sync Now. \`docs/testing-with-fake-onedrive.md\` has the details.
- Synthetic clicks work: \`brew install cliclick\`, then \`cliclick c:1038,13\` opens the status item's menu, and clicking the icon again closes it. Coordinates are in points; screenshots shown to agents are downscaled, so take coordinates from \`-R\` region captures, in which each pixel is half a point. Do not use osascript System Events UI scripting, because it hangs. \`docs/testing-with-fake-onedrive.md\` lists the other pitfalls.
- \`mac_read_file\` sometimes reports a file that was just written as missing, and returns an earlier image when a path is reused. Use a new name under \`/private/tmp\` for each screenshot, and retry the read once.
- Never point the app at real OneDrive data or rclone credentials from an orb or satellite.
$end_marker
EOF

mv "$tmp" "$guidance_file"
echo "Wrote orb guidance to $guidance_file"
